/-!
# Tag 063M: an immersion is quasi-regular iff its conormal algebra is the symmetric algebra

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be an immersion of schemes.  [Stacks, Tag 063M] says that `i` is quasi-regular
if and only if

1. `i` is locally of finite presentation,
2. the conormal sheaf `𝒞_{Z/X}` is finite locally free, and
3. the canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` of [Stacks, Tag 0632] is an isomorphism.

The direction out of quasi-regularity is proved clause by clause elsewhere: condition (1) in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.FinitePresentation`, condition (2) in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.ConormalLocallyFree`, condition (3) in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersion.ConormalSymmetricIso`, which also proves the
converse *over one affine chart*.  This file supplies the step that turns those four statements
into the `iff`: the **shrinking step**, which produces out of (1) and (2) around every point of
`Z` an affine closed-immersion chart whose chart ideal is generated by exactly as many functions
as the conormal sheaf has free generators there.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegularImmersion_iff`: **[Stacks, Tag 063M]**, the whole statement.
* `Stacks.Conormal.exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_of_isFiniteLocallyFree`: the shrinking step —
  out of conditions (1), (2) and (3), every point of `Z` lies in the preimage of an affine
  closed-immersion chart whose chart ideal is generated by a quasi-regular sequence.
* `Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_exists_quasiRegular_affineChart`: the affine-chart
  criterion, the converse of `Stacks.Conormal.exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_mem`.
* `Stacks.Conormal.exists_affineChart_basis_conormalPiece`: condition (2) read on a chart — a
  finite locally free conormal sheaf has a *free* module of degree-one sections over an affine
  closed-immersion chart around each point, inside any prescribed neighbourhood.
* `Stacks.Conormal.fg_chartIdeal_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation`: condition (1) read on a chart —
  the chart ideal is finitely generated.
* `Stacks.Conormal.exists_sub_one_mem_mul_mem_of_fg_of_le_sup_sq`: Nakayama's lemma in the form
  the shrinking step uses it.
* `Stacks.Conormal.chartIdeal_map_of_le`: the chart ideal of a smaller affine open inside a
  chart is the image of the chart ideal.

## Implementation notes

**The shrinking does not shrink the source.**  The open the shrinking step produces is a basic
open `D(r)` of the chart with `r ∈ 1 + I`, so `r` restricts to `1` on `Z` and
`i⁻¹ᵁ D(r) = i⁻¹ᵁ U` as opens of `Z`.  That is what makes the argument cheap: the basis of
`Γ(𝒞_{Z/X}, i⁻¹U)` obtained from condition (2) is a basis over the shrunk chart *verbatim*, with
no localisation of modules and no comparison of ranks.  Only the ideal changes, and it changes by
`Stacks.Conormal.chartIdeal_map_of_le` together with the invertibility of `r` on `D(r)`.

**Where each condition enters.**  Condition (2) gives the rank `c` and the basis; lifting that
basis along the degree-one presentation `Stacks.Conormal.ConormalAlgebraData.localMap` of the
chart gives `c` functions with `I = (f) + I²` and nothing more.  The passage to `I = (f)` is
Nakayama's lemma, which needs `I` finitely generated, and that is condition (1) — through local
finite presentation of the surjection `Γ(X, U) ↠ Γ(Z, i⁻¹U)` on an affine chart.  Condition (3)
is used only at the very end, by `Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegular_chart_of_isIso`.

**The criterion is Tag 063G on the canonical open.**  Quasi-regularity of an immersion is
quasi-regularity of the defining ideal sheaf of its closed factor `i.liftCoborder` on
`i.coborderRange`; `AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy` turns that
into the existence of affine opens of `i.coborderRange` carrying quasi-regular generating
sequences, and an affine chart of `X` is such an affine open through
`Stacks.Conormal.coborderAffineChart`, with `Stacks.Conormal.coborderSectionEquiv` carrying the
sequence across.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.5 (Tag 063M)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063M)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.2 (Tag 0632)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0632)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.2 (Tag 063G)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 00DV (Nakayama)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

universe u

namespace Stacks.Conormal

/-- **Nakayama's lemma in the form the shrinking step of [Stacks, Tag 063M] needs.**  Let `I` be
a finitely generated ideal of a commutative ring and `J` an ideal with `I ⊆ J + I²`.  Then some
`r ∈ 1 + I` multiplies `I` into `J`; consequently `I` and `J` agree after inverting `r`.

Apply `Submodule.exists_sub_one_mem_and_smul_eq_zero_of_fg_of_le_smul` to the image `N` of `I` in
`R ⧸ J`: the hypothesis `I ⊆ J + I²` says exactly that `N ⊆ I • N`, because a class in `N` is
the class of an element of `I²`, and `N` is finitely generated because `I` is. -/
theorem exists_sub_one_mem_mul_mem_of_fg_of_le_sup_sq {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I J : Ideal R)
    (hfg : I.FG) (hIJ : I ≤ J ⊔ I ^ 2) :
    ∃ r : R, r - 1 ∈ I ∧ ∀ a ∈ I, r * a ∈ J := by
  have hNfg : (Submodule.map J.mkQ I).FG := Submodule.FG.map (f := J.mkQ) hfg
  have hle : Submodule.map J.mkQ I ≤ I • Submodule.map J.mkQ I := by
    rintro x ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp (hIJ ha)
    have hy0 : J.mkQ y = 0 := (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero J).mpr hy
    have hz2 : z ∈ I • I := by rwa [Ideal.smul_eq_mul, ← pow_two]
    have : J.mkQ (y + z) = J.mkQ z := by rw [map_add, hy0, zero_add]
    rw [this, ← Submodule.map_smul'']
    exact Submodule.mem_map_of_mem hz2
  obtain ⟨r, hr1, hr2⟩ :=
    Submodule.exists_sub_one_mem_and_smul_eq_zero_of_fg_of_le_smul I _ hNfg hle
  refine ⟨r, hr1, fun a ha => ?_⟩
  have h := hr2 (J.mkQ a) (Submodule.mem_map_of_mem ha)
  rw [← map_smul] at h
  exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero J).mp h

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **A finite locally free conormal sheaf has a free module of degree-one sections over an
affine closed-immersion chart around each point.**  The chart may be taken inside any
prescribed open neighbourhood of the point in `Z`.

Finite local freeness of `𝒞_{Z/X}` transports to the degree-one piece of the conormal algebra
along `Stacks.Conormal.conormalDegreeOneIso`, and in its pointwise form it trivialises the piece
over some open `UZ` of `Z` around the point; an affine closed-immersion chart whose preimage
lies inside `UZ` exists by `Stacks.Conormal.exists_affineChart_mem`, the trivialisation
restricts to the spectrum of the functions on that preimage, and a trivialisation of the sheaf
associated with a module is a basis of that module. -/
theorem exists_affineChart_basis_conormalPiece (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (hflf : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (conormalSheaf i))
    (V : Z.Opens) (z : Z) (hz : z ∈ V) :
    ∃ (U : X.affineOpens), IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl) ∧
      ∃ (_ : z ∈ i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) (_ : i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ V) (c : ℕ),
      Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin c) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) := by
  have hqc : (conormalPiece i 1).IsQuasicoherent := (conormalAlgebra i).isQuasicoherent 1
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (conormalPiece i 1) :=
    @AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.of_iso _ _ _
      (conormalDegreeOneIso i) hflf
  obtain ⟨UZ, hzUZ, I, hIfin, ⟨e⟩⟩ :=
    (Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFree_iff (conormalPiece i 1)).mpr inferInstance z
  obtain ⟨U, hzU, hUle, hUcob⟩ := exists_affineChart_mem i (UZ ⊓ V) z ⟨hzUZ, hz⟩
  have hU := AlgebraicGeometry.isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_coborderRange i U.1 hUcob
  have hVaff : IsAffineOpen (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := isAffineOpen_preimage_affineChart i U hU
  have hr : Set.range hVaff.fromSpec.base ⊆ Set.range UZ.ι.base := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.coe_opensRange, hVaff.opensRange_fromSpec, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact hUle.trans inf_le_left
  obtain ⟨e'⟩ := Stacks.Modules.nonempty_restrictIsoFree_of_range_subset UZ.ι hVaff.fromSpec
    (conormalPiece i 1) I hr e
  obtain ⟨b⟩ := (tilde_fixed_free_iff_basis Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
    Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) I).mp
    ⟨Stacks.Modules.tildeIsoRestrictFromSpec (conormalPiece i 1) hVaff ≪≫ e'⟩
  exact ⟨U, hU, hzU, hUle.trans inf_le_right, Nat.card I, ⟨b.reindex (Finite.equivFin I)⟩⟩

/-- **Lifting a finite spanning family of the degree-one conormal sections to functions on the
chart.**  Over an affine closed-immersion chart `U` with chart ideal `I`, a family of `c`
sections of `𝒞_{Z/X}` spanning `Γ(𝒞_{Z/X}, i⁻¹U)` lifts to `c` functions in `I` which generate
`I` *modulo `I²`*.

The sections of `𝒞_{Z/X}` over the chart are `I/I²` through
`Stacks.Conormal.ConormalAlgebraData.localMap` in degree one, which is surjective with kernel
`I²`; a representative of a spanning section is the required function, and a coefficient of the
spanning relation is lifted along `i.app U`, surjective because the chart is a closed-immersion
chart. -/
theorem exists_mem_le_span_sup_sq_of_span_eq_top (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) {c : ℕ}
    (b : Module.Basis (Fin c) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) :
    ∃ f : Fin c → Γ(X, U.1), (∀ k, f k ∈ chartIdeal i U) ∧
      chartIdeal i U ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range f) ⊔ chartIdeal i U ^ 2 := by
  classical
  have hψ : Function.Surjective (i.app U.1).hom :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.app_surjective_of_closedRestriction i U hU
  choose a ha using fun k : Fin c => (conormalAlgebra i).localMap_surjective U hU 1 (b k)
  refine ⟨fun k => ((a k : Γ(X, U.1))), fun k => by simpa using (a k).2, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  set xm : ↥(chartIdeal i U ^ 1) := ⟨x, by simpa using hx⟩ with hxm
  set t := (conormalAlgebra i).localMap U hU 1 xm with ht
  choose r hr using fun k : Fin c => hψ (b.repr t k)
  have hLw : (conormalAlgebra i).localMap U hU 1 (∑ k, r k • a k) = t := by
    rw [map_sum, Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ =>
      ((conormalAlgebra i).localMap_smul U hU 1 (r k) (a k) (r k • a k)
        (by rw [SetLike.val_smul, smul_eq_mul])).trans (by rw [ha k, hr k])]
    exact b.sum_repr t
  have hmem2 : x - ∑ k, r k * (a k : Γ(X, U.1)) ∈ chartIdeal i U ^ 2 := by
    have h1 := ((conormalAlgebra i).localMap_eq_zero_iff U hU 1
      (xm - ∑ k, r k • a k)).mp (by rw [map_sub, hLw, sub_self])
    have hcoe : ((xm - ∑ k, r k • a k : ↥(chartIdeal i U ^ 1)) : Γ(X, U.1))
        = x - ∑ k, r k * (a k : Γ(X, U.1)) := by
      rw [Submodule.coe_sub, Submodule.coe_sum]
      simp [hxm, smul_eq_mul]
    rw [hcoe] at h1
    simpa using h1
  refine Submodule.mem_sup.mpr ⟨∑ k, r k * (a k : Γ(X, U.1)), ?_,
    x - ∑ k, r k * (a k : Γ(X, U.1)), hmem2, by ring⟩
  exact Ideal.sum_mem _ fun k _ => Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨k, rfl⟩)

/-- A smaller affine open inside an affine closed-immersion chart is again a chart. -/
private theorem isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_of_isClosedImmersion_resLE (i : Z ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion i] {U : X.affineOpens}
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) {U' : X.affineOpens}
    (hle : U'.1 ≤ U.1) : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U'.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U'.1) le_rfl) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_coborderRange i _
    (hle.trans (le_coborderRange_of_isClosedImmersion_resLE i U.1 hU))

/-- The image of the ideal spanned by a family is spanned by the image of the family. -/
private theorem map_span_range {R S ι F : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [FunLike F R S]
    [RingHomClass F R S] (g : F) (f : ι → R) :
    Ideal.map g (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) = Ideal.span (Set.range fun k => g (f k)) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-- **The chart ideal of a smaller affine open inside an affine closed-immersion chart is the
image of the chart ideal.**  Both are read on the canonical open `i.coborderRange`, where the
chart ideal is a component of the ideal sheaf `Scheme.Hom.ker` of the closed factor: the
compatibility of the components of an ideal sheaf with restriction is one of its structure
fields, and `Stacks.Conormal.coborderSectionEquiv` carries it back to the charts, naturally in
the containment. -/
theorem chartIdeal_map_of_le (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (U U' : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) (hle : U' ≤ U) :
    chartIdeal i U' = Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom (chartIdeal i U) := by
  have hle' : U'.1 ≤ U.1 := hle
  have hU' := isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_of_isClosedImmersion_resLE i hU hle'
  have hW : coborderAffineChart i U' hU' ≤ coborderAffineChart i U hU := by
    change (coborderAffineChart i U' hU').1 ≤ (coborderAffineChart i U hU).1
    rw [coborderAffineChart_coe, coborderAffineChart_coe]
    exact fun x hx => hle' hx
  have hnat : X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op ≫ i.coborderRange.ι.app U'.1 =
      i.coborderRange.ι.app U.1 ≫
        i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op := by
    rw [i.coborderRange.ι.naturality (homOfLE hle).op]
    rfl
  have hnat_elem : ∀ a : Γ(X, U.1),
      coborderSectionEquiv i U' hU' ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom a)
        = (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom
            (coborderSectionEquiv i U hU a) := by
    intro a
    have h := congrArg (fun φ : Γ(X, U.1) ⟶ _ => φ.hom a) hnat
    simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply] at h
    rw [coborderSectionEquiv_apply, coborderSectionEquiv_apply]
    exact h
  have hmapW : Ideal.map (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom
      ((coborderIdeal i).ideal (coborderAffineChart i U hU))
      = (coborderIdeal i).ideal (coborderAffineChart i U' hU') :=
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal (coborderIdeal i) hW
  refine le_antisymm (fun b hb => ?_) (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha => ?_)
  · have hkey : (coborderIdeal i).ideal (coborderAffineChart i U' hU')
        ≤ Ideal.map (coborderSectionEquiv i U' hU')
          (Ideal.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom (chartIdeal i U)) := by
      rw [← hmapW]
      refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx => ?_
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := (coborderSectionEquiv i U hU).surjective x
      exact Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (hnat_elem a ▸ Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _
        (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ((coborderSectionEquiv_mem_ideal i U hU a).mpr hx)))
    exact Ideal.apply_mem_of_equiv_iff.mp
      (hkey ((coborderSectionEquiv_mem_ideal i U' hU' b).mp hb))
  · refine (coborderSectionEquiv_mem_ideal i U' hU' _).mpr ?_
    rw [hnat_elem a, ← hmapW]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ((coborderSectionEquiv_mem_ideal i U hU a).mp ha)

/-- **The chart ideal of an immersion locally of finite presentation is finitely generated.**
Over an affine closed-immersion chart the map on functions is a surjection of finite
presentation — of finite presentation because `i` is and both opens are affine, surjective
because the chart is a closed-immersion chart — and the kernel of a surjection between algebras
of finite presentation is finitely generated.

This is the only use the criterion of [Stacks, Tag 063M] makes of its condition (1), and it is
what Nakayama's lemma needs. -/
theorem fg_chartIdeal_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (hfp : LocallyOfFinitePresentation i) (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) :
    (chartIdeal i U).FG := by
  have hVaff : IsAffineOpen (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := isAffineOpen_preimage_affineChart i U hU
  have hfp' := AlgebraicGeometry.HasRingHomProperty.appLE
    (Q := RingHom.FinitePresentation) @LocallyOfFinitePresentation i hfp U
    ⟨i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1, hVaff⟩ le_rfl
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app] at hfp'
  let := (i.app U.1).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) := hfp'
  exact Algebra.FinitePresentation.ker_fG_of_surjective
    (Algebra.ofId Γ(X, U.1) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
    (AlgebraicGeometry.app_surjective_of_closedRestriction i U hU)

/-- **The affine-chart criterion for a quasi-regular immersion.**  If every point of `Z` lies in
the preimage of an affine open of `X` over which `i` restricts to a closed immersion and whose
chart ideal is generated by a quasi-regular sequence, then `i` is a quasi-regular immersion.

This is the converse of `Stacks.Conormal.exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_mem`, and it is the
`KerGeneratedBy` form of [Stacks, Tag 063G] applied to the canonical closed factor: the range of
`i.liftCoborder` is closed, so a point of its closure is the image of a point of `Z`; the affine
chart of `X` around it is an affine open of `i.coborderRange` by
`Stacks.Conormal.coborderAffineChart`, and `Stacks.Conormal.coborderSectionEquiv` carries the
chart ideal and its generating sequence there. -/
theorem isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_exists_quasiRegular_affineChart (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (h : ∀ z : Z, ∃ (U : X.affineOpens),
      IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl) ∧ ∃ (_ : z ∈ i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) (c : ℕ)
      (f : Fin c → Γ(X, U.1)), chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span (Set.range f) ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular Γ(X, U.1) (List.ofFn f)) :
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsQuasiRegularImmersion i := by
  refine (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf_iff_kerGeneratedBy
    i.liftCoborder).mpr fun x hx => ?_
  rw [i.liftCoborder.isClosedEmbedding.isClosed_range.closure_eq] at hx
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hzU, c, f, hspan, hqr⟩ := h z
  refine ⟨coborderAffineChart i U hU, ?_, c, fun k => coborderSectionEquiv i U hU (f k), ?_,
    isQuasiRegular_ringEquiv (coborderSectionEquiv i U hU) f hqr⟩
  · have hpre : i.liftCoborder ⁻¹ᵁ (coborderAffineChart i U hU).1 = i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 :=
      coborderAffineChart_preimage i U hU
    exact show z ∈ i.liftCoborder ⁻¹ᵁ (coborderAffineChart i U hU).1 from hpre ▸ hzU
  · rw [← coborderIdeal_ideal, ← coborderSectionEquiv_map_ideal i U hU, hspan, map_span_range]

/-! ### The shrinking step -/

/-- **The shrinking step of [Stacks, Tag 063M].**  Out of conditions (1) and (2) — `i` locally of
finite presentation and `𝒞_{Z/X}` finite locally free — every point of `Z` lies in the preimage
of an affine closed-immersion chart whose chart ideal is generated by *exactly as many* functions
as the conormal sheaf has free generators there; with condition (3) that generating sequence is
quasi-regular.

Condition (2) gives a chart on which `Γ(𝒞_{Z/X}, i⁻¹U)` is free of some rank `c`, and lifting a
basis gives `c` functions with `I = (f) + I²` only
(`Stacks.Conormal.exists_mem_le_span_sup_sq_of_span_eq_top`).  Nakayama's lemma upgrades this to
`r · I ⊆ (f)` for some `r ∈ 1 + I`, using that `I` is finitely generated — which is condition
(1), through `Stacks.Conormal.fg_chartIdeal_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation`.  Over the basic open
`D(r)` the function `r` becomes invertible, so there `I` *is* generated by the images of the `f`;
and `D(r)` is a shrinking of the chart that does not shrink its preimage at all, because `r`
restricts to `1` on `Z`, so the basis of the conormal sections survives verbatim.  The chart
converse `Stacks.Conormal.isQuasiRegular_chart_of_isIso` then applies. -/
@[sga "1 II 4.14" "(a)"]
theorem exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_of_isFiniteLocallyFree (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (hfp : LocallyOfFinitePresentation i)
    (hflf : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (conormalSheaf i))
    (hiso : ∀ n : ℤ, IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app n)) (z : Z) :
    ∃ (U : X.affineOpens), IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl) ∧
      ∃ (_ : z ∈ i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) (c : ℕ) (f : Fin c → Γ(X, U.1)),
      chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span (Set.range f) ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsQuasiRegular Γ(X, U.1) (List.ofFn f) := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hzU, -, c, ⟨b⟩⟩ :=
    exists_affineChart_basis_conormalPiece i hflf ⊤ z trivial
  obtain ⟨f, hfmem, hfle⟩ := exists_mem_le_span_sup_sq_of_span_eq_top i U hU b
  obtain ⟨r, hr1, hr2⟩ := exists_sub_one_mem_mul_mem_of_fg_of_le_sup_sq (chartIdeal i U)
    (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (fg_chartIdeal_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation i hfp U hU) hfle
  have hle : X.affineBasicOpen r ≤ U := X.affineBasicOpen_le r
  have hU' := isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_of_isClosedImmersion_resLE i hU hle
  have hres1 : (i.app U.1).hom r = 1 := by
    have h0 : (i.app U.1).hom (r - 1) = 0 := hr1
    rw [map_sub, map_one, sub_eq_zero] at h0
    exact h0
  have hpre : i ⁻¹ᵁ (X.affineBasicOpen r).1 = i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 := by
    change i ⁻¹ᵁ X.basicOpen r = i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1
    rw [Scheme.preimage_basicOpen, hres1, Scheme.basicOpen_one]
  have hunit : IsUnit ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom r) :=
    X.toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen r
  have hspan : chartIdeal i (X.affineBasicOpen r) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun k => (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom (f k)) := by
    rw [chartIdeal_map_of_le i U (X.affineBasicOpen r) hU hle]
    have hmapspan := map_span_range (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom f
    refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha => ?_) ?_
    · have hmul : (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom (r * a) ∈
          Ideal.span (Set.range fun k => (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op).hom (f k)) := by
        rw [← hmapspan]
        exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (hr2 a ha)
      rw [map_mul] at hmul
      exact (Ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem _ hunit).mp hmul
    · rw [← hmapspan]
      exact Ideal.map_mono (Ideal.span_le.mpr fun _ ⟨k, hk⟩ => hk ▸ hfmem k)
  have hb' : Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin c) Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ (X.affineBasicOpen r).1)
      Γ(conormalPiece i 1, i ⁻¹ᵁ (X.affineBasicOpen r).1)) := by
    rw [hpre]; exact ⟨b⟩
  obtain ⟨b'⟩ := hb'
  exact ⟨X.affineBasicOpen r, hU', hpre ▸ hzU, c, _, hspan,
    isQuasiRegular_chart_of_isIso i (X.affineBasicOpen r) hU' _ hspan b' hiso⟩

/-! ### Tag 063M -/

/-- An immersion `i : Z ⟶ X` of schemes is quasi-regular **if and only if** (1) it is locally of
finite presentation, (2) its conormal sheaf `𝒞_{Z/X}` is finite locally free, and (3) the
canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` of [Stacks, Tag 0632] is an isomorphism in every
degree. -/
@[stacks 063M "the whole statement: an immersion is quasi-regular iff it is locally of finite \
presentation, its conormal sheaf is finite locally free, and the map of 0632 is an isomorphism",
  ega "IV 16.9.8" "(i)", ega "IV 17.12.1", ega "IV 19.1.3"]
theorem isQuasiRegularImmersion_iff (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] :
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsQuasiRegularImmersion i ↔
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation i ∧
        AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (conormalSheaf i) ∧
          ∀ n : ℤ, IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app n) := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ⟨locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isQuasiRegularImmersion i h,
    isFiniteLocallyFree_conormalSheaf_of_isQuasiRegularImmersion i h,
    fun n => isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app i h n⟩, fun h => ?_⟩
  exact isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_exists_quasiRegular_affineChart i
    (exists_quasiRegular_affineChart_of_isFiniteLocallyFree i h.1 h.2.1 h.2.2)

end Stacks.Conormal

